# Kept out of the distributed archive.
#
# Entries are exact relative file paths -- modkit matches them literally, so a
# bare "tests/" silently does nothing. Add the file, not the directory.

# The suite requires engine test infrastructure (tests.modkit) and engine
# modules (src.world.Collision, src.world.gen2.World), which is a private
# require against the shipped package, and `pack` treats warnings as fatal.
# It only means anything inside an engine checkout.
tests/rby_run_forrest_test.lua

# The two end-to-end drivers reach tests/drivers/util.lua, which lives in the
# engine and not here, and are run through POKEPORT_DRIVER against a checkout.
# Same reason as the suite above: outside one they are unrunnable files taking
# up room in a player's install.
tests/drivers/route4_climb_test.lua
tests/drivers/gold_climb_test.lua

# The README's six frames.
#
# They stay in the repo, because a GitHub page nobody installs is exactly
# where they belong: they are what makes the feature legible to someone
# deciding whether to try it. They do not go in an archive this project
# distributes, because a screenshot of a running game is composited out of
# tiles, sprites and font glyphs decoded from the player's OWN ROM -- it is
# ROM-derived content wearing a .png extension, and `modkit lint` does not
# catch it because it reads data files rather than pictures.
#
# The cost is that README.md, which does ship, points at six images the
# archive does not carry. That is the right way round: a player who installs
# the mod reads it on GitHub, where the images resolve, and the alternative
# is shipping the pictures.
#
# .github/workflows/release.yml drops docs/ wholesale for the same reason, so
# a release .zip and a `modkit pack` archive contain the same files.
docs/images/gen1-climb-1-before.png
docs/images/gen1-climb-2-midair.png
docs/images/gen1-climb-3-after.png
docs/images/gen2-climb-1-before.png
docs/images/gen2-climb-2-midair.png
docs/images/gen2-climb-3-after.png
